<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gjakova</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Đakovica, Djakovica</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gjakova, in Serbian Đakovica, is a city in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosovo">Kosovo</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metohija">Metohija</a> plain near the Albanian border. It grew in the Ottoman period around a market and the Hadum Mosque. Montenegro took it in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-balkan-war">First Balkan War</a> of 1912–1913, and it later became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a>. Its population is mainly Albanian, and its old bazaar was badly damaged in the Kosovo War of 1999.</p></div>
